@startuml
!theme plain
autonumber

participant "Gateway\n(StartAllProvidersHandler)" as GW
queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "Provider A\nSimulator" as PA
participant "Provider B\nSimulator" as PB

== After Phase 1 (SystemReady) ==

GW -> GW: PublishStartProviders()\n→ StartAllProvidersCommand

alt Production mode
  GW -> GW: Load AutoStart providers from DB
  GW -> GW: Docker API: start containers\n(for each provider)
  GW -> GW: Task.Delay(3000) — wait for\ncontainer RabbitMQ setup
else Development mode
  note over GW
    Containers already running via\ndocker-compose — no orchestration
  end note
end

== Await Provider Responses (AsyncAwaiter) ==

note over GW
  AsyncAwaiter creates temp queue,\nbinds to ProviderRoutingKeys.ProviderStarted,\nthen publishes broadcast ping
end note

GW -> MQ: Publish RequestAllProviderStartedCommand\n(broadcast to all providers)
MQ -> PA: Deliver RequestAllProviderStarted
MQ -> PB: Deliver RequestAllProviderStarted

PA -> PA: Initialize, load capabilities
PA -> MQ: Publish ProviderStartedEvent\n(Provider data)
PB -> PB: Initialize, load capabilities
PB -> MQ: Publish ProviderStartedEvent\n(Provider data)

MQ -> GW: Deliver ProviderStartedEvent (A)
GW -> GW: Match — collect response
MQ -> GW: Deliver ProviderStartedEvent (B)
GW -> GW: Match — collect response\nCompletionCondition: all IDs received ✓

== Announce Complete ==

GW -> MQ: Publish AllProvidersStartedEvent

@enduml
